  "id": "home-cage",
  "term": "home cage",
  "definition": "In this research context, a home cage is the animal’s usual living enclosure where it is housed between tests. The term is used to distinguish features available in that everyday housing environment, such as access to a running wheel, from conditions during separate social-behavior testing.",
